+## Usage reported to afterModelResponse
+
+`afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits, and the usage it is handed covers every provider call the orchestrator made in that turn, not only the last one, so a deployer recording a billing line or an audit entry from the hook counts the rounds that carried the question and the tool results (re-cinq/HALEngine#93).
+
+- A turn that ran two tool rounds reports the sum of all three provider calls' token counts ([validated by: reports the sum of three provider calls when a turn runs two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L58)).
+- A round that reports no usage is skipped rather than poisoning the total: the rounds that reported are still summed, and a turn in which no round reported usage reports `undefined` ([validated by: counts the rounds that reported usage when one round reports none, and reports nothing when no round did](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L68)).
+- A turn that called no tools reports exactly the usage of its single provider call, so the common path does not move ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+- Round usage records are summed field by field: `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens` are each added independently ([validated by: sums two usage records field by field](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L32)).
+- Adding usage to an empty accumulator returns the new record unchanged, so the first round that reports usage seeds the running total correctly ([validated by: returns the second when accumulator is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L36)).
+- A round that reports no usage leaves the running total unchanged, so a silent round does not reset the accumulated count to zero ([validated by: returns the accumulator when next is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L40)).
+- When no round in the turn reported usage the total is `undefined`, not zero or `NaN` ([validated by: returns undefined when both are undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L44)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
